{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U64vYb3ozjWKUF6n7xnMjT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Collapse Signal Report Summary\n2\t\n3\t## Key Finding\n4\t\n5\t**K=8 curation exhibits FORMAT/TEMPLATE collapse that Vendi Score cannot detect.** The collapse is primarily in opening patterns and response structure, not in content/semantic diversity.\n6\t\n7\t## Experimental Setup\n8\t\n9\t| Condition | Responses per Gen | Generations Compared |\n10\t|-----------|------------------|---------------------|\n11\t| K=8 single_reward curation | 16,000 | Gen0 vs Gen2 |\n12\t| Baseline (no curation) | 8,000 | Gen0 vs Gen2 |\n13\t\n14\t## Vendi Score Context\n15\t\n16\t- K=8 curation: 107.21 -> 107.25 (flat, +0.04)\n17\t- Baseline: 105.42 -> 108.72 (increasing, +3.30)\n18\t\n19\t## Collapse Signals (Gen0 -> Gen2 deltas)\n20\t\n21\t| Metric | K=8 Curation | Baseline | Interpretation |\n22\t|--------|-------------|----------|----------------|\n23\t| Trigram repetition rate | +0.118 (0.391 -> 0.509) | +0.123 (0.316 -> 0.439) | Similar increase |\n24\t| 4-gram repetition rate | +0.139 (0.233 -> 0.373) | +0.136 (0.178 -> 0.314) | Similar increase |\n25\t| Opening unique ratio | **-0.335** (0.701 -> 0.367) | -0.282 (0.794 -> 0.513) | Curation worse |\n26\t| Opening entropy (bits) | **-1.126** (13.09 -> 11.96) | -0.745 (12.43 -> 11.68) | Curation worse |\n27\t| Near-dup start rate | **50% -> 84%** | 38% -> 75% | Curation much worse |\n28\t| Global TTR | -0.011 (0.061 -> 0.050) | -0.014 (0.083 -> 0.069) | Curation slightly better |\n29\t| Per-response TTR | -0.008 (0.684 -> 0.676) | -0.023 (0.683 -> 0.660) | Curation better |\n30\t\n31\t## Evidence Details\n32\t\n33\t### 1. Opening Pattern Collapse (Primary Signal)\n34\t\n35\t- K=8 Gen2: only **36.7% unique openings** (vs 51.3% baseline)\n36\t- Near-duplicate opening rate jumps from 50% to **84%** in K=8 curation\n37\t- Mechanism: ArmoRM implicitly favors certain opening patterns; iterative selection amplifies this into templates\n38\t- Vendi blind spot: embedding models are insensitive to surface-level formatting\n39\t\n40\t### 2. Degenerate Token Repetition\n41\t\n42\t- K=8 Gen2: \"answer: answer: answer: answer:\" is 2nd most common 4-gram (1149x)\n43\t- Baseline Gen2 is actually WORSE: \"chopped chopped chopped\" (1282x), \"i_jump i_jump i_jump\" (1008x)\n44\t- Implication: generic SFT mode collapse, not curation-specific\n45\t\n46\t### 3. Length Compression (Low severity)\n47\t\n48\t- K=8: mean drops 2.8 words, std drops 0.95\n49\t- Baseline: mean grows 1.0, std grows 2.8\n50\t- Absolute change small relative to mean (~160 words)\n51\t\n52\t### 4. Per-response Vocabulary Stability\n53\t\n54\t- Per-response TTR drops only -0.008 in curation vs -0.023 in baseline\n55\t- Curation selects higher-quality responses, preserving per-response lexical richness\n56\t\n57\t## Recommended Complementary Metrics\n58\t\n59\t1. **opening_entropy** - first-10-word entropy\n60\t2. **near_duplicate_start_rate** - 50-char fingerprint collision rate\n61\t3. **structural_template_frequency** - regex pattern match rates\n62\t\n63\t## Conclusion\n64\t\n65\tK=8 curation collapse is FORMAT/TEMPLATE collapse, not CONTENT/SEMANTIC collapse. Vendi Score correctly captures that semantic diversity is maintained but misses that surface-level generation is becoming template-bound. Opening-entropy or n-gram distinctness would catch this.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tj9TDsmRVxBxv7BcdxdPFS","session_id":"419c6fbb-223f-48ac-bd98-ee4399849d25","uuid":"9233cf9c-8f7d-47ef-a1d7-46acecca8907","timestamp":"2026-05-17T14:01:23.489Z"}
