{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HfAyq4odNYV11T5HigTAms","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# C1 vs C5 Format Diversity Analysis\n2\t\n3\t**C1**: LoRA K=4, ArmoRM top-1 curated (`carr_quick_probe_03`)\n4\t**C5**: LoRA K=4, no curation baseline (`carr_baseline_no_curation_01`)\n5\t\n6\t## Status\n7\t\n8\t- C5 metrics: **COMPLETE**\n9\t- C1 metrics: **IN PROGRESS** (re-running on bjb2-23165 GPU 0, ETA ~18:00 CST May 17)\n10\t  - C1 data was overwritten by C5 baseline run (shared output dir). Re-generating to `outputs_lora_k4_curated/`.\n11\t  - Watcher script will auto-compute and save to `analysis/c1_c5_format_diversity.json` on completion.\n12\t\n13\t## Results\n14\t\n15\t| Metric | C1 Gen0 | C1 Gen2 | C5 Gen0 | C5 Gen2 | C1 delta | C5 delta |\n16\t|--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|----------|----------|\n17\t| opening_unique_ratio | — | — | 0.7532 | 0.4789 | — | -0.2743 |\n18\t| opening_entropy (bits) | — | — | 12.4257 | 11.6803 | — | -0.7454 |\n19\t| near_duplicate_start_rate | — | — | 0.3827 | 0.7489 | — | +0.3662 |\n20\t| per_response_ttr | — | — | 0.6828 | 0.6598 | — | -0.0230 |\n21\t| trigram_repetition_rate | — | — | 0.1739 | 0.2576 | — | +0.0837 |\n22\t\n23\t## Metric Definitions\n24\t\n25\t1. **opening_unique_ratio**: fraction of responses with unique 50-char prefix (higher = more diverse)\n26\t2. **opening_entropy**: Shannon entropy of first-10-token sequence distribution (bits; higher = more diverse)\n27\t3. **near_duplicate_start_rate**: fraction of responses whose 50-char prefix is shared with at least one other response (lower = more diverse)\n28\t4. **per_response_ttr**: mean type-token ratio per individual response (higher = richer vocabulary)\n29\t5. **trigram_repetition_rate**: fraction of distinct trigrams appearing >=2 times across corpus (lower = more diverse)\n30\t\n31\t## C5 Observations\n32\t\n33\tC5 (baseline, no curation) shows significant format collapse over 3 generations:\n34\t- Opening diversity drops 36% (0.753 → 0.479 unique ratio)\n35\t- Near-duplicate starts nearly double (38% → 75%)\n36\t- Trigram repetition increases +8.4pp\n37\t- Per-response vocabulary degrades mildly (-0.023 TTR)\n38\t\n39\tThis confirms baseline SFT self-improvement without curation already causes format collapse. The key question is whether C1 (reward curation) makes it worse or better.\n40\t\n41\t## Data Paths (server bjb2-23165)\n42\t\n43\t- C5: `/root/autodl-tmp/carr/outputs/gen_{0,2}/condition_0/generations.json`\n44\t- C1 (regenerating): `/root/autodl-tmp/carr/outputs_lora_k4_curated/gen_{0,2}/condition_0/generations.json`\n45\t- Combined metrics JSON: `/root/autodl-tmp/carr/analysis/c1_c5_format_diversity.json`\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"419c6fbb-223f-48ac-bd98-ee4399849d25","uuid":"5458ff24-2f59-4a2e-ba37-5fdc585621b7","timestamp":"2026-05-17T14:03:13.955Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/collapse_aware_reward_rebalancing/artifacts/c1_vs_c5_format_analysis.md","content":"# C1 vs C5 Format Diversity Analysis\n\n**C1**: LoRA K=4, ArmoRM top-1 curated (`carr_quick_probe_03`)\n**C5**: LoRA K=4, no curation baseline (`carr_baseline_no_curation_01`)\n\n## Status\n\n- C5 metrics: **COMPLETE**\n- C1 metrics: **IN PROGRESS** (re-running on bjb2-23165 GPU 0, ETA ~18:00 CST May 17)\n  - C1 data was overwritten by C5 baseline run (shared output dir). Re-generating to `outputs_lora_k4_curated/`.\n  - Watcher script will auto-compute and save to `analysis/c1_c5_format_diversity.json` on completion.\n\n## Results\n\n| Metric | C1 Gen0 | C1 Gen2 | C5 Gen0 | C5 Gen2 | C1 delta | C5 delta |\n|--------|---------|---------|---------|---------|----------|----------|\n| opening_unique_ratio | — | — | 0.7532 | 0.4789 | — | -0.2743 |\n| opening_entropy (bits) | — | — | 12.4257 | 11.6803 | — | -0.7454 |\n| near_duplicate_start_rate | — | — | 0.3827 | 0.7489 | — | +0.3662 |\n| per_response_ttr | — | — | 0.6828 | 0.6598 | — | -0.0230 |\n| trigram_repetition_rate | — | — | 0.1739 | 0.2576 | — | +0.0837 |\n\n## Metric Definitions\n\n1. **opening_unique_ratio**: fraction of responses with unique 50-char prefix (higher = more diverse)\n2. **opening_entropy**: Shannon entropy of first-10-token sequence distribution (bits; higher = more diverse)\n3. **near_duplicate_start_rate**: fraction of responses whose 50-char prefix is shared with at least one other response (lower = more diverse)\n4. **per_response_ttr**: mean type-token ratio per individual response (higher = richer vocabulary)\n5. **trigram_repetition_rate**: fraction of distinct trigrams appearing >=2 times across corpus (lower = more diverse)\n\n## C5 Observations\n\nC5 (baseline, no curation) shows significant format collapse over 3 generations:\n- Opening diversity drops 36% (0.753 → 0.479 unique ratio)\n- Near-duplicate starts nearly double (38% → 75%)\n- Trigram repetition increases +8.4pp\n- Per-response vocabulary degrades mildly (-0.023 TTR)\n\nThis confirms baseline SFT self-improvement without curation already causes format collapse. The key question is whether C1 (reward curation) makes it worse or better.\n\n## Data Paths (server bjb2-23165)\n\n- C5: `/root/autodl-tmp/carr/outputs/gen_{0,2}/condition_0/generations.json`\n- C1 (regenerating): `/root/autodl-tmp/carr/outputs_lora_k4_curated/gen_{0,2}/condition_0/generations.json`\n- Combined metrics JSON: `/root/autodl-tmp/carr/analysis/c1_c5_format_diversity.json`\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}}}
